{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":482006,"name":"","username":"_Remi","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/_/a9adbd/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-03T08:44:48.884Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482006-describe-the-bug-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482006-describe-the-bug-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter updating to 0.36.0: messsag \u003ccode\u003eCan't reach your computer\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nOptions ‘Retry’ or ‘Recover computer’ fail.\u003cbr\u003e\nThere was no  change in my network; similar bugreports suggest nslookup and subsequent modification of network settings, but lookup results seem fine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482006-steps-to-reproduce-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482006-steps-to-reproduce-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate to 0.36.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482006-expected-behavior-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482006-expected-behavior-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLoading bots normally\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482006-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482006-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"video-placeholder-container\" data-video-src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/c/a/ca84fead1d82c0f42025b16bfaf2f52d609dd775.mp4\"\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/b/8/b8c143224d1e5c2077663a7ed1daee54773ec89e.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/qmpUQYooBZn6xyvwLE9b6xyeUd8.png?dl=1\" title=\"Cursor DNS lookup.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/b/8/b8c143224d1e5c2077663a7ed1daee54773ec89e.png\" alt=\"Cursor DNS lookup.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"qmpUQYooBZn6xyvwLE9b6xyeUd8\" width=\"353\" height=\"500\" data-dominant-color=\"161616\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eCursor DNS lookup.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e405×573 14.7 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482006-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482006-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482006-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482006-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.36.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482006-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482006-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-03T09:05:33.389Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":14,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":56.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":170438,"topic_slug":"grokbot-fails-after-update-cant-reach-your-computer","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135741,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grokbot-fails-after-update-cant-reach-your-computer/170438/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true,"can_vote":false},{"id":482069,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-03T09:44:37.012Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report. Good news: your computer and bots are OK and reachable. The issue isn’t with them or with your network.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat happened: the Grok Bot desktop app is still using a login session from before you changed your Cursor password on September 2. Changing your password ends all existing sessions, so every request from the app gets rejected after that, and it shows it as “Can’t reach your computer”. The update to 0.36.0 just installed on top of that and isn’t the cause. Your DNS is fine too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo fix it, sign out in the desktop app and sign back in:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Grok Bot, click your name or avatar in the bottom left of the sidebar.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelect Sign out and confirm.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign in again with your Cursor account using the new password.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait about a minute after signing in. The bots should load.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you don’t see Sign out in that menu, right-click the Grok Bot icon in the system tray, choose Quit, reopen the app, and try again. You don’t need Recover computer or Reset here. The computer itself is fine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if it still won’t connect after you sign in again.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-03T09:44:37.012Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":15,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":36.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":170438,"topic_slug":"grokbot-fails-after-update-cant-reach-your-computer","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grokbot-fails-after-update-cant-reach-your-computer/170438/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":true,"topic_accepted_answer":true},{"id":482101,"name":"","username":"_Remi","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/_/a9adbd/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-03T10:21:22.404Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSigning out and signing in again resolved my problem.\u003cbr\u003e\nIt might be helpfull to automatically log out in such case and show the user he/she should login again.\u003cbr\u003e\nThanks!\u003cbr\u003e\nRem